<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_12" targetNamespace="https://kitchen406.local/bpmn">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_12">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_12" name="BPMN-12 | Preparing-Owner Assignment and Allocation Validation" processRef="Process_12" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_12" name="Preparing-Owner Assignment and Allocation Validation" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>BPMN-13 invokes this process during Mark Ready. One instance handles one fulfillment, including one subscription week. If there is no valid saved allocation, the Admin/Owner or Staff member selects preparing owners per product line in the Ready confirmation. Commit the allocation and its audit history in the same transaction as Ready. This is the only assignment point. Existing valid assignments, including those retained after a status reversal, are reused. Later pickup, courier or cake handoff workflows can validate saved allocations without prompting. Authentication is upstream in BPMN-26. Stale version, invalid allocation and lock failures are shown on the main diagram. Batch Ready applies these checks and reports outcomes independently for each fulfillment.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_12">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_16_user" name="Admin/Owner or Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Edit_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Confirm_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Cancel_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_16_system" name="Kitchen406 System — Fulfillment Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Load_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Mode_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Version_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>VersionValid_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>VersionError_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Allocation_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>AllocationValid_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>AllocationError_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Lock_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>LockValid_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>LockError_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>LockRejected_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>SaveMode_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Validated_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Commit_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Saved_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Success_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Reject_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Recovery_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>ReturnError_16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_16" name="Mark Ready or check saved assignments">
      <bpmn:documentation>Begin with a Mark Ready request or a downstream saved-allocation check. Historical completed records without an allocation remain Unallocated.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Load_16" name="Load fulfillment details and saved owner assignments">
      <bpmn:documentation>Read product-line identities and full quantities, eligible baking owners, saved percentages, expected/current version, status and courier lock state. Scope is one operational fulfillment, including one subscription week; the prepaid subscription purchase is not an allocation unit. Staff sees operational selections/percentages only, never allocated sales, costs, estimated profit or restricted analytics (FR-STAFF-06). On refresh, use the latest saved version and require fresh review and confirmation of any draft. Never replay a stale submission automatically.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_31</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Mode_16" name="New assignment needed for Ready?" default="Flow_16_4">
      <bpmn:documentation>Select owners only during Mark Ready and only when the fulfillment lacks a valid saved allocation. For a repeated Ready transition or a downstream check, use saved allocations and skip selection.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Edit_16" name="Select preparing owners and splits in Mark Ready">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-FUL-16-17,24. Display saved choices and whole line quantities. Select eligible Owner A at 100%, Owner B at 100%, or both. Newly selecting both proposes 50/50; allow Owner A an integer 1-99 and set B to 100 minus A. Apply-to-all affects only this fulfillment: retain and display existing per-line splits when applying both, using 50/50 only where no prior both-owner split exists. Review every affected line before confirmation. Selecting a single owner gives that owner 100%. The acting account is never assigned a share automatically. Locked records must not accept normal editing; a stale or forged draft is rejected by server validation. Cancel leaves all saved values unchanged.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_5</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_30</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Confirm_16" name="Confirm Mark Ready?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Cancel_16" name="Cancelled; saved state unchanged">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_6</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Version_16" name="Compare submitted and current order versions">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-FUL-23; NFR-SEC-14. Detect a stale submitted version and flag the request for refresh.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="VersionValid_16" name="Order version current?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_13</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="VersionError_16" name="Explain what changed since review">
      <bpmn:documentation>Explain that the submitted version is stale and prompt for a refresh when applicable.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Allocation_16" name="Check eligible owners and percentages on every line">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-FUL-16-18,24,26. Every product line requires exactly one valid allocation for the whole line quantity. Only the two eligible baking owners: A alone=100/0, B alone=0/100, both=integer A 1..99 and B=100-A. New both-owner selection defaults to 50/50; apply-to-all preserves and displays existing both-owner splits for review. Use the Ready draft for a new assignment and saved values for later validation. Staff action never implies a share. Historical completed items remain Unallocated, not retroactively inferred.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_16</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="AllocationValid_16" name="All line allocations valid?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_17</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_19</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="AllocationError_16" name="Explain missing/invalid assignments or percentages">
      <bpmn:documentation>Show affected lines and what needs correction. The Mark Ready confirmation can correct a rejected draft. Return saved-allocation validation failures to the caller without opening an editor.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_18</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Lock_16" name="Check Ready eligibility and courier locks">
      <bpmn:documentation>A new assignment requires Preparing status, a Mark Ready request and no active or unresolved courier booking. Ready and later actions reuse saved assignments. For saved-allocation validation, check lock compatibility with the requested fulfillment action.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_20</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="LockValid_16" name="Requested action allowed by locks?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_20</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_21</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_23</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="LockError_16" name="Explain completion or courier lock">
      <bpmn:documentation>Identify the current status or courier lock that blocks the requested action. Recheck it on a later attempt.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_21</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_22</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="LockRejected_16" name="Rejected: requested action locked">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_22</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="SaveMode_16" name="New Ready assignment?">
      <bpmn:documentation>A newly confirmed Ready draft proceeds to the combined commit. A valid saved allocation returns the checked version for the caller?s protected action.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_23</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_24</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_25</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Validated_16" name="Saved assignments validated">
      <bpmn:documentation>Return the saved allocation and checked version to the invoking Ready or downstream workflow. Recheck the version and applicable controls at that workflow?s commit.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_24</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Commit_16" name="Commit allocations and history with Ready via BPMN-13">
      <bpmn:documentation>Recheck version, lock state and per-line validity. Save the allocation, actor, timestamp and previous/new values with the Ready status and version in the atomic commit in BPMN-13. Reject a failed transaction without saving a partial allocation or status. Replay an already successful operation without duplicating history.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_25</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_26</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Saved_16" name="Commit successful?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_26</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_27</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_28</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Success_16" name="Ready and owner assignments saved">
      <bpmn:documentation>Return the saved per-line allocations and Ready version. Reuse these assignments for later fulfillment actions and reporting.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_27</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Reject_16" name="Explain why allocations could not be saved">
      <bpmn:documentation>Report the exact failure, including version, allocations, locks or save errors.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_28</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_29</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Recovery_16" name="How can this request recover?" default="Flow_16_32">
      <bpmn:documentation>Within a Mark Ready confirmation, correct a rejected draft or refresh after a stale version or retryable write error. Reloading may reveal a valid saved allocation, in which case selection is skipped. Saved-allocation checks return their rejection to the caller.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_29</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_30</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_31</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16_32</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="ReturnError_16" name="Request blocked">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16_32</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_1" sourceRef="Start_16" targetRef="Load_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_2" sourceRef="Load_16" targetRef="Mode_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_3" sourceRef="Mode_16" targetRef="Edit_16" name="Yes">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">markReady and not(validSavedAllocation)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_4" sourceRef="Mode_16" targetRef="Version_16" name="No — validate existing allocations" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_5" sourceRef="Edit_16" targetRef="Confirm_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_6" sourceRef="Confirm_16" targetRef="Cancel_16" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_7" sourceRef="Confirm_16" targetRef="Version_16" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_12" sourceRef="Version_16" targetRef="VersionValid_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_13" sourceRef="VersionValid_16" targetRef="VersionError_16" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_14" sourceRef="VersionError_16" targetRef="Recovery_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_15" sourceRef="VersionValid_16" targetRef="Allocation_16" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_16" sourceRef="Allocation_16" targetRef="AllocationValid_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_17" sourceRef="AllocationValid_16" targetRef="AllocationError_16" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_18" sourceRef="AllocationError_16" targetRef="Recovery_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_19" sourceRef="AllocationValid_16" targetRef="Lock_16" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_20" sourceRef="Lock_16" targetRef="LockValid_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_21" sourceRef="LockValid_16" targetRef="LockError_16" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_22" sourceRef="LockError_16" targetRef="LockRejected_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_23" sourceRef="LockValid_16" targetRef="SaveMode_16" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_24" sourceRef="SaveMode_16" targetRef="Validated_16" name="No — validation only" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_25" sourceRef="SaveMode_16" targetRef="Commit_16" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_26" sourceRef="Commit_16" targetRef="Saved_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_27" sourceRef="Saved_16" targetRef="Success_16" name="Yes" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_28" sourceRef="Saved_16" targetRef="Reject_16" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_29" sourceRef="Reject_16" targetRef="Recovery_16" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_30" name="Correct allocations" sourceRef="Recovery_16" targetRef="Edit_16">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">markReadyRequest and assignmentAllowed and invalidAllocations</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_31" name="Refresh and review" sourceRef="Recovery_16" targetRef="Load_16">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">markReadyRequest and (staleVersion or retryableWriteFailure)</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16_32" name="Stop request" sourceRef="Recovery_16" targetRef="ReturnError_16" />
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="References_16">
      <bpmn:text>Owner allocation rules
One owner: 100%. Both owners: initially 50/50; Owner A integer 1–99%, Owner B the remainder.
Apply-to-all keeps existing both-owner line splits for review.
Staff is the action performer, never an automatic recipient.

Reuse boundaries
BPMN-26: authentication precondition.
BPMN-13: select once in Mark Ready and commit together.
BPMN-14/15/17: check saved assignments as needed.
Validation-only follows the visible checks without prompting for edits.
Batch: validate and report each fulfillment separately.
Failed or cancelled requests leave saved data unchanged.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Association_16" sourceRef="Edit_16" targetRef="References_16" associationDirection="None" />
  </bpmn:process>
